.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_CTRL 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_ctrl ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_callback_ctrl ,
.Nm SSL_ctrl ,
.Nm SSL_callback_ctrl
.Nd internal handling functions for SSL_CTX and SSL objects
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft long
.Fo SSL_CTX_ctrl
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int cmd"
.Fa "long larg"
.Fa "void *parg"
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo SSL_CTX_callback_ctrl
.Fa "SSL_CTX *"
.Fa "int cmd"
.Fa "void (*fp)()"
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo SSL_ctrl
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "int cmd"
.Fa "long larg"
.Fa "void *parg"
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo SSL_callback_ctrl
.Fa "SSL *"
.Fa "int cmd"
.Fa "void (*fp)()"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Xr SSL_*_ctrl 3
family of functions is used to manipulate settings of the SSL_CTX and
SSL objects.
Depending on the command
.Fa cmd
the arguments
.Fa larg ,
.Fa parg ,
or
.Sy fp
are evaluated.
These functions should never be called directly.
All functionalities needed are made available via other functions or
macros.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The return values of the
.Xr SSL*_ctrl 3
functions depend on the command supplied via the
.Fa cmd
parameter.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7
